  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponses int&#xe9;gr&#xe9;es aux besoins urgents des personnes d&#xe9;plac&#xe9;es de force et des communaut&#xe9;s via l&#x2019;approche communautaire dans les r&#xe9;gions de Tillab&#xe9;ri et Diffa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this UNHCR project is to improve the protection environment for communities in the communes of T&#xe9;ra, Ayorou, Chetimari and N&apos;Guigmi by profiling the population, responding to protection needs and strengthening community involvement. The project provides intervention to improve the protection environment for the forcibly displaced people and host community members, strengthened capacity-building to promote resilience such as multi-purpose cash transfer and community-based protection against risks linked to explosive engines. The intervention provides humanitarian assistance to 151,359 people (34,497 men, 36,224 women and 80,638 children), including 1,270 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
